<title>LITHUANIA: Yields rise on 91-day Lithuanian T-bills.</title>
<headline>Yields rise on 91-day Lithuanian T-bills.</headline>
<dateline>VILNIUS 1997-07-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>The average yield on 91-day Lithuanian Treasury bills rose on Monday to 9.04 percent from 8.96 percent at the last auction, the central bank said.</p>
<p>Amounts are in millions of litas unless otherwise stated.</p>
<p> MATURITY  AV YIELD  (LAST) MIN/MAX YIELD ISSUE  BID     SOLD</p>
<p> 91-day    9.04	 8.96  8.70/9.18     50.0   66.923  50.0</p>
<p>The settlement date for the auction is July 24 and the bills mature on October 23.</p>
<p>The next auction will be held on Tuesday, when 50 million litas of 182-day paper will be offered.</p>
<p>-- Andrius Vilkancas, Vilnius newsroom +370 2 22 35 17</p>
</text>
